### 2. Controlled Instantiation I - The FBA Statistic is NOT `kappa_V`

> **Definition 3.21* [Discrete FBA proxy, rename].** Let `S` be a stoichiometric model with feasible polytope `F = {v: Sv=0, l<=v<=u}` and wild-type optimum `v^{wt}` maximizing `v_bio`. Fix an embedding
> ```
> iota: F -> B
> ```
> `C^1` on strata, with `d iota_v: T_v F -> T_{iota(v)} B`. Fix `V = iota({v: v_bio < (1-delta)v_bio^{wt}})`. Define the **FBA curvature proxy**:
> ```
> K_V^{FBA}(v; tau,beta,D) := sum_{r in R} 1_{r essential}(v) * [ (v_r - v_r^{wt})^2 / E(iota(v)) ]
> ```
> or any norm you actually computed, with **explicit essentiality mask** `1_{r essential}(v) = 1` iff `max{v_bio: v_r=0} < (1-delta)v_bio^{wt}`.
